# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Microsoft 365 Copilot Cost Management MCP — configuration
#
# The server talks to Microsoft Graph (beta) under /copilot/costManagement.
# Pick ONE authentication method below. All other variables are optional.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Auth option A: raw bearer token (pass-through) ───────────────────────────
# Easiest for testing or when another process already minted a Graph token.
# The token must carry the CopilotCostManagement-* scopes for the operations
# you intend to call. Note: tokens expire (~60–90 min) and are NOT refreshed.
# GRAPH_ACCESS_TOKEN=eyJ0eXAiOiJ...

# ── Auth option B: app-only (client credentials) ─────────────────────────────
# Works only for operations that support APPLICATION permissions:
#   - getTenantCreditBalance
#   - service & funding usage reports
# Grant CopilotCostManagement.Read.All (+ -Reports.Read.All) as application
# permissions with admin consent in Microsoft Entra.
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret

# ── Auth option C: delegated (interactive device code) ───────────────────────
# Works for ALL operations (most are delegated-only). Set tenant + client id but
# NO secret; the server prints a device-code prompt to stderr on first token use.
# The signed-in admin must hold the right directory role (e.g. Billing/AI Admin).
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ── Optional overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Graph host (default https://graph.microsoft.com)
# GRAPH_BASE_URL=https://graph.microsoft.com
# Graph API version (default beta — the only version this API ships in today)
# GRAPH_API_VERSION=beta
# OAuth scope requested from the credential (default https://graph.microsoft.com/.default)
# GRAPH_SCOPE=https://graph.microsoft.com/.default

# Safety: when true, only read-only tools are registered (no create/update/
# delete/approve/reject). Great for giving an agent observability without risk.
# COPILOT_COST_MGMT_READONLY=false
